 hethirdplace.is/event/cacurrent1105\n\nJoin Aleesa Pitchamarn Alexander\, 
 the Robert M. and Ruth L. Halperin Associate Curator of Modern and Contemp
 orary Art\, on this special tour of California Current: Art and Histories 
 from the Bay Area.\n\nRSVP here.\n\nHow does a community stay rooted in a 
 region that’s constantly changing? California Current invites you to con
 sider this question and others through its more than 60 works — many on 
 view for the first time — that explore the interplay between Bay Area hi
 story\, art\, and artists over the past century.\n\nTitled after the major
  cold-water current that runs the length of the West Coast of North Americ
 a\, California Current brings together paintings\, sculptures\, works on p
 aper\, photographs\, and time-based media by Bay Area artists from the twe
 ntieth century to the present. The exhibition traces a series of interconn
 ected currents — ecological\, infrastructural\, technological\, personal
 \, creative\, and political — that have shaped both artistic production 
 and everyday life in Northern California.\n\nArranged thematically across 
 time and media\, California Current places historical works in conversatio
 n with contemporary ones\, emphasizing both continuity and change. Togethe
 r\, they ask: What has drawn so many people to this region? What has allow
 ed communities and creative practices to take root here? And what continue
 s to keep so many of us — despite the Bay Area’s contradictions\, pres
 sures\, and constant reinvention — deeply connected to this place? Prese
